  "rules": [
    "Select by user's actual goal and mechanisms, not only keywords; keyword matching is a shortlist not a conclusion.",
    "Keep research knowledge active; do not equate scope inventory with completed evidence.",
    "Use one canonical source per fact and link, never copy the 152 unit bodies into this index.",
    "Read only relevant files first; source/validation specialists are called when the task needs them.",
    "Cross-branch engineering paths are candidates requiring explicit checkout; a link is not runtime invocation.",
    "No private keys, trading, signing, paid API or x402 payment without authorization.",
    "Authority for work method: current-operating-guidance.md first; legacy progression/continuity stage checklists are optional historical methods, not compulsory actions or outputs.",
    "Literal routes and expert_lens_ids are optional candidate pointers; for abstract explanations no expert invocation is required; consult one domain source or extend to external source when it could change the answer.",
    "For multi-hop shared-service versus common-control questions prioritize D05 economic actor and original signed transaction/source evidence; for provider reuse prioritize capability/contract/price/privacy before market inference.",
